static.solution:
\rho=8, \theta=\frac{2 \pi}{3}, and \phi=\frac{11 \pi}{6}. The relations between the spherical and rectangular coordinates imply
\begin{array}{rcl}
x \amp  = \amp  \rho \sin\phi \cos\theta = 8 \sin \frac{11 \pi}{6} \cos \frac{2 \pi}{3} = 8 \cdot \frac{-1}{2} \cdot \frac{-1}{2} \\
y \amp  = \amp  \rho \sin\phi \sin\theta = 8 \sin \frac{11 \pi}{6} \sin \frac{2 \pi}{3} = 8 \cdot \frac{-1}{2} \cdot \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \\
z \amp  = \amp  \rho \cos\phi = 8 \cos \frac{11 \pi}{6}=8 \cdot \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}
\end{array}
